Right, so... honestly? Most of this stuff wouldn't change what I buy. I already know energy drinks and chocolate aren't exactly health food—everyone knows that. The graphic pictures of diseased eyes and tumours sound like they'd just wind me up, to be fair. That's the kind of preachy stuff I was talking about. And the calorie counts? I mean, I'd glance at them, but if I fancy a Dairy Milk, a number on the wrapper isn't going to stop me, especially if it's the same price as the fruit pot. The only thing that might actually make a dent is if I'm already thinking about it, or if the warnings made me feel a bit guilty enough to switch one time out of five, maybe.

