*sits back, scratches chin*

Look, I'm not going to pretend I'm some paragon of virtue here. I eat what I fancy most days, and if I want a chocolate bar, I'll have one. The warnings about cancer and heart disease—that's all noise to me, to be honest. Everyone's got to die of something, and I've made it this far doing more or less what I please. The graphic photos sound like the sort of thing designed to wind people up on social media, more theatre than anything else. As for calorie counts, I can work that out myself if I cared, but I don't really sit there doing sums. What *would* actually make me think twice is if I could see at a glance that something's got half the calories of something else—that's practical, not preachy.

